<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-March 4.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-March 4.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for March 4</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Mar    203 50    208.00    210.50     222.50</p>
<p>    Apr    201.50    206.00    208.50     222.50</p>
<p>    May    201.50    206.00    208.50     222.50</p>
<p>    Jun    200.50    205.00    207.50     222.50</p>
<p>    Jul    199.00    203.50    206.00     221.00</p>
<p>    Aug    198.00    202.50    205.00     220.00</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$2.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	171.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  146.50	    Port Adelaide	 148.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     146.75	    Port Giles	    148.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	144.50	    Wallaroo		148.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    143.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     146.50	    Port Lincoln	  149.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   147.00	    Thevenard	     144.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 146.00	     Esperance	    151.25</p>
<p>    Portland	147.00	     Albany		 152.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    154.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    152.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
